ui/gtk: do not refresh more often than every 30 ms

gd_update_monitor_refresh_rate() takes the refresh interval from the
monitor, capped at 30 ms from above only, so on a 144 Hz laptop panel the
GTK console refreshed every 7 ms. With ramfb, which has no dirty tracking,
every refresh uploads the whole 1080x2400 surface (10 MB) with the BQL
held: the main loop held the BQL two thirds of the time and every vCPU
exit, exception return and I/O register access queued behind it, while
the guest (iOS) only draws 30 frames per second. Use the monitor's
interval only when it is longer than GUI_REFRESH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT.
Based on QEMU v11.1.2.

diff --git a/ui/gtk.c b/ui/gtk.c
index 7078d89..6174fea 100644
--- a/ui/gtk.c
+++ b/ui/gtk.c
@@ -810,9 +810,15 @@ void gd_update_monitor_refresh_rate(VirtualConsole *vc, GtkWidget *widget)
 
     gd_set_ui_refresh_rate(vc, refresh_rate);
 
-    /* T = 1 / f = 1 [s*Hz] / f = 1000*1000 [ms*mHz] / f */
+    /*
+     * T = 1 / f = 1 [s*Hz] / f = 1000*1000 [ms*mHz] / f, but never shorter
+     * than GUI_REFRESH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT: a refresh redraws the whole surface
+     * of a display without dirty tracking (ramfb) with the BQL held, and at
+     * the 144 Hz of a laptop panel that kept the main loop, and so every vCPU
+     * waiting for the BQL, busy two thirds of the time.
+     */
     vc->gfx.dcl.update_interval = refresh_rate ?
-        MIN(1000 * 1000 / refresh_rate, GUI_REFRESH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT) :
+        MAX(1000 * 1000 / refresh_rate, GUI_REFRESH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT) :
         GUI_REFRESH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT;
 #endif
 }
